WEBVTT

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:02.350
Well, let's get crackin'.

00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:03.580
Let's-a-go.

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:05.850
Stop messing around and start!

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:08.990
The ambiguous 3cm?
Does that mean it's plushy? Wait!

00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:12.330
The wrapping is a uniform, argh,
it's not an act, pooh

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:13.890
Gotta do your best, gotta just do it

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:15.530
That's time to catch 'n' release, eek

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:17.190
Between sweat (whoop)
sweat (whoop)

00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:20.600
Darlin', darlin', freeze!

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:26.580
Kinda lethargic,
something's kinda comin' out

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:28.550
I love you... Oh wait,
one of those was different

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:29.780
Worrywarts, high metal bars

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:31.580
Tasty thoughts... And that's enough!

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:33.390
The heated body of that
flying you-know-who

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:34.920
It's what you call a normal girlie

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:36.130
Am I the only one surprised?

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:37.390
Seconds on pork-bone broth ramen
with wire-hard noodles

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:38.320
Da da da da da

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:46.360
Pom-poms cheer squad

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:47.930
Let's get cherry pie

00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:49.570
Happy fun welcoming party

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:51.140
Look up! Sensation

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:54.140
Yeah! Feeling of existence,
dot dot small planet

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:55.740
Collided and it melted away,
in total awe

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:57.510
Go all out to sing, shi-ranger!

00:00:57.510 --> 00:00:58.680
Take it away!

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:03.150
I should be the one who'll be
laughing in the end

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:10.360
Because I have the sailor suit
<- This is my conclusion

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:12.360
It's only Monday!

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:15.910
Already in a bad mood? What to do?

00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:22.870
I really prefer the summer outfits
<- kya! wah! good! (cute!)

00:01:22.870 --> 00:01:25.920
Until we approach 3 pixels,
no hesitations please *

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:27.540
Do your best, be energetic

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:29.730
My darlin', darlin' please!

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:31.750
Right?

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:33.080
Doesn't it stink?

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:34.500
Sure does!

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:37.920
Golden Week's almost over...

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:40.510
Did you already take care of your homework?

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:43.720
Not yet actually...

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:48.060
You know how you can't help having fun on long vacations?

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:49.230
We're in trouble now!

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:50.770
Right, Sis?

00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:51.980
Sorry.

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:54.300
I'm almost done.

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:56.900
<i>But you've been playing with me the whole time...</i>

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:17.170
I'm done eating.

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:23.130
I have a
question about this part...

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:26.100
How would I know
the answers if you don't?

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:27.390
Aren't you in college?!

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:31.810
Go wake up Tsukasa already.

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:32.520
No way.

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:33.730
She's not gonna wake up.

00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:36.810
Wake up already!

00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:39.680
Dad and Sis sure are late.

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:42.070
Didn't they have a ground—
breaking ceremony this morning?

00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:43.200
What...

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:43.650
...time is it?

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:44.320
I'm home.

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:45.620
It's already noon.

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:46.280
Welcome home.

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:49.040
Good morning...

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:50.450
It's already past noon.

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:52.290
I can't believe how
you can sleep so much.

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:56.710
Did you see the special final episode of Apron of Love last night?

00:02:56.710 --> 00:02:57.630
Nope.

00:02:57.630 --> 00:02:59.310
I fell asleep halfway through.

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:00.530
You were asleep?

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:02.670
It got really crazy!

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:05.340
A guy balanced a red wash basin on top of his head at the end!

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:16.660
Kagami!

00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:18.840
You have a call from Miyuki-chan!

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:19.860
Okay.

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:24.110
Would you like to hold a study
session for checking homework answers?

00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:25.560
Sounds great!

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:26.450
Let's do that!

00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:27.700
Kagami!

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:29.830
You have a call from Konata-chan!

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:33.710
How about we do a study session for finishing off homework?

00:03:33.710 --> 00:03:34.620
Wait one sec!

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:37.330
You're just going to copy my answers, aren't you?!

00:03:37.330 --> 00:03:39.920
So let me copy your homework.

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:41.300
Right to the point, huh?

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:43.760
You can copy them...

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:45.260
...but if you don't do the homework yourself...

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:48.180
...you'll totally bomb the test after vacation.

00:03:48.590 --> 00:03:50.190
You're right...

00:03:50.190 --> 00:03:52.310
We'll only end up hurting ourselves...

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:55.350
I'm good at winging stuff the night before so I'll be fine.

00:03:55.350 --> 00:03:56.040
So let me copy.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:57.730
At least pretend to be guilty!

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:01.020
I'm sorry to intrude.

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:01.440
Oh, welcome!

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:02.980
Welcome!

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:03.610
Oh.

00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:05.610
Are you also here to study, Izumi-san?

00:04:05.610 --> 00:04:06.110
No.

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:07.450
She's just copying.

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:09.220
Anyway...

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:10.830
You've barely touched it.

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:14.120
What were you doing during break?

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:15.710
Um...

00:04:17.170 --> 00:04:19.080
Twenty-three pages of math...

00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:20.040
Twenty pages of world history...

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:20.840
Finally made it to
the Imperial Gate.

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:22.800
Thirty pages of English...

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:23.210
Finally made it to
the Imperial Gate.

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:26.470
We have five days of vacation.

00:04:26.470 --> 00:04:27.680
Assuming five
hours spent a day...

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:29.450
No, four hours...

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:33.010
That means 1.15
pages of math an hour.

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:35.430
Getting a lot more
experience than I expected.

00:04:35.430 --> 00:04:36.680
Oh no!

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:37.100
I haven't done
any work today!
Getting a lot more
experience than I expected.

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:38.270
I haven't done
any work today!

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:38.980
Wonder how much
more I need for a level.

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:40.230
Um...

00:04:40.230 --> 00:04:41.860
I have three days left...

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:42.650
So let's go with six hours a day?

00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:44.230
Found a loincloth!

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:47.030
Nobody remembers the name
of the guy who spent ten years...

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:47.200
...watching over
new workers.

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:49.320
This is starting
to get really slow.

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:50.160
It's Yutaka.

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:50.200
This is starting
to get really slow.

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:50.570
Well, I'm almost maxed out.

00:04:50.570 --> 00:04:51.740
Two days left!

00:04:51.740 --> 00:04:53.280
If I cram for the
last two days...

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:54.540
So all that's left is...

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:57.250
Golden Week's almost over...

00:04:57.250 --> 00:04:59.580
Did you already take
care of your homework?

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:03.710
How about we do a study
session for finishing off homework?

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:07.380
I wanted to do everything just as planned...

00:05:07.380 --> 00:05:08.840
Mission failed.

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:10.430
Shouldn't have even bothered.

00:05:10.430 --> 00:05:11.680
You're even worse!

00:05:20.570 --> 00:05:23.540
<i>So she ended up doing it herself, huh?</i>

00:05:24.020 --> 00:05:27.850
<i>I guess she's still a hard-working girl deep down.</i>

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:33.700
<i>But her accuracy rate is too much for me to bear!</i>

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:34.290
<i>Pathetic...</i>

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:35.660
<i>Just pathetic!</i>

00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:36.920
Howdy!

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:38.750
Did y'all have a fun vacation?

00:05:38.890 --> 00:05:40.040
Then again...

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:41.620
You had bunches of homework...

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:43.790
...and a test right after vacation...

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:46.750
...so you couldn't've been having fun the whole time.

00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:49.670
It barely felt like a vacation.

00:05:49.670 --> 00:05:50.550
So sad.

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:52.640
Too bad I just let loose and had a blast!

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:53.470
Teacher.

00:05:54.010 --> 00:05:56.180
I also let loose and had a blast!

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:56.600
Hey.

00:05:58.430 --> 00:06:01.810
Aren't these things designed so you can never get anything?

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:03.850
Depends on what you're going for.

00:06:03.850 --> 00:06:06.150
Some things are especially hard to grab.

00:06:06.820 --> 00:06:07.690
Right?

00:06:07.690 --> 00:06:09.530
I could never bring myself to touch one of these machines.

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:15.200
Incredible!

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:15.910
Nah.

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:17.620
I already knew this one was gettable.

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:19.620
<i>So maybe...</i>

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:21.790
<i>...if I went after that one...</i>

00:06:21.790 --> 00:06:23.120
I might actually get it.

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:24.920
Is that what you're thinking?

00:06:25.380 --> 00:06:27.300
Nope! No way!

00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:28.750
B-But...

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:30.050
...I guess I'll give it a try.

00:06:30.050 --> 00:06:30.920
So you wanna.

00:06:30.920 --> 00:06:32.300
Go for it, Sis!

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:38.850
Thought I had it...

00:06:38.850 --> 00:06:39.940
Too bad...

00:06:42.410 --> 00:06:43.130
Huh?

00:06:48.110 --> 00:06:48.690
No way!

00:06:49.060 --> 00:06:49.570
Why?!

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:51.820
A great person once said...

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:54.280
...that operating a UFO catcher is like opening a savings accounts.

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:56.070
Smart guy...

00:06:59.330 --> 00:06:59.940
Not again!

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:00.580
Screwed up!

00:07:03.910 --> 00:07:04.210
Here are your scores!

00:07:04.210 --> 00:07:05.420
I was hopeless...

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:06.920
You achieved Taiko Rank 1!

00:07:06.920 --> 00:07:07.420
You've got a great sense of rhythm, Kona-chan.

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:09.000
You achieved Taiko Rank 5!

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:09.340
Nah.

00:07:09.340 --> 00:07:09.380
You achieved Taiko Rank 5!

00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:11.210
It's got nothing to do with rhythm.

00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:16.640
The skills you pick up from gaming
end up being pretty useless in real life.

00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:19.010
You're living proof of that.

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:40.120
You're strong, Kona-chan.

00:07:40.120 --> 00:07:41.330
Pretty much.

00:07:41.330 --> 00:07:44.120
<i>How much time has she spent on this stuff?</i>

00:07:44.120 --> 00:07:45.530
Izumi?

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:48.380
Izumi's absent today?

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:49.880
Ms. Kuroi.

00:07:49.880 --> 00:07:51.590
You have a call from Izumi-san.

00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:52.480
Yes.

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:54.350
It's me.

00:07:54.350 --> 00:07:55.840
Teacher, I'm terribly sorry...

00:07:55.840 --> 00:07:57.930
...but I need to take a sick day...

00:07:57.930 --> 00:07:59.860
That's unusual, Izumi.

00:07:59.860 --> 00:08:00.600
Did ya catch a cold?

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:01.250
No.

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:02.930
It's a bad case of May sickness.

00:08:03.270 --> 00:08:05.230
I can barely move...

00:08:05.230 --> 00:08:06.600
Just get your behind down here!

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:10.190
Hey!

00:08:10.190 --> 00:08:11.250
We're leaving.

00:08:13.730 --> 00:08:16.690
Why is your bag so full?

00:08:16.690 --> 00:08:18.440
Testing starts tomorrow...

00:08:18.440 --> 00:08:21.660
...so I have to take everything home for an all-nighter.

00:08:21.660 --> 00:08:22.660
Don't tell me...

00:08:22.660 --> 00:08:25.080
...you're going to cram all that tonight?

00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:26.620
Honestly...

00:08:26.620 --> 00:08:29.550
Waiting till the day before a test to take your textbooks home...

00:08:29.550 --> 00:08:31.090
...is way too late!

00:08:31.660 --> 00:08:34.260
But this is how I always wing it.

00:08:34.260 --> 00:08:36.080
You sure sound confident.

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:36.580
Well.

00:08:36.580 --> 00:08:39.050
Show me how good you really are then.

00:08:48.830 --> 00:08:49.770
Okay!

00:08:49.770 --> 00:08:52.250
Time to return your tests!

00:08:53.360 --> 00:08:54.190
I want my mommy!

00:08:54.320 --> 00:08:55.570
So-so, I guess.

00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:57.120
How'd you do?

00:08:57.120 --> 00:08:58.900
You probably shouldn't ask...

00:08:58.900 --> 00:09:00.320
I worked hard though...

00:09:00.610 --> 00:09:01.320
Well, now...

00:09:01.320 --> 00:09:02.450
What about Miss All-nighter?

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:03.870
Just fine. Thanks for asking.

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:04.990
That's just wrong!

00:09:10.460 --> 00:09:11.500
So tired...

00:09:11.500 --> 00:09:13.500
I don't feel like doing anything...

00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:14.130
Come on.

00:09:14.130 --> 00:09:15.130
Let's go.

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:20.130
But you still ended up wandering around with us, huh?

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:21.890
Comp Festival!

00:09:21.890 --> 00:09:23.510
Discount on all QUO cards!

00:09:23.510 --> 00:09:24.810
Gotta collect 'em all!

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:25.640
Okay.

00:09:25.640 --> 00:09:26.960
Time to get a job.

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:28.810
You're so easy to read.

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:32.190
Seriously...

00:09:32.190 --> 00:09:36.070
I've never heard of anyone being absent for May sickness.

00:09:36.070 --> 00:09:38.070
I can understand how she feels though.

00:09:38.070 --> 00:09:39.900
Doesn't it say sickness in the name?

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:41.780
Shouldn't it count as a serious disease?

00:09:41.780 --> 00:09:43.320
Do you seriously mean that?

00:09:44.990 --> 00:09:47.580
What exactly is May sickness again?

00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:49.210
Miyuki.

00:09:49.210 --> 00:09:50.250
Tell her.

00:09:50.250 --> 00:09:51.620
Let's see...

00:09:51.620 --> 00:09:53.500
It begins with the feeling of achievement one experiences...

00:09:53.500 --> 00:09:56.800
...after accomplishing a major goal such
as getting into college or getting a new job.

00:09:56.800 --> 00:10:01.260
When new relationships beginning in
April don't work out as well as you'd like...

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:03.840
...you are unable to keep up with the gap...

00:10:03.840 --> 00:10:06.180
...between the new life you imagined and reality.

00:10:06.180 --> 00:10:09.180
As a result, you feel helpless and weary.

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:14.020
So plain lethargy might not be considered May sickness...

00:10:14.020 --> 00:10:16.570
'Sides, it's got nothing to do with...

00:10:16.570 --> 00:10:18.440
...second-years in high school like us.

00:10:18.440 --> 00:10:22.450
I'm always pumped by the change of pace in spring.

00:10:22.450 --> 00:10:23.700
Oh, really.

00:10:23.900 --> 00:10:25.990
Still, while I'm not as bad as Konata...

00:10:25.990 --> 00:10:28.240
...I do feel unusually tired this time of year.

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:30.200
Once I'm home...

00:10:30.200 --> 00:10:32.330
...I can't bring myself to do homework.

00:10:32.330 --> 00:10:33.790
Me too!

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:39.050
Nobody's gonna comment?

00:10:41.970 --> 00:10:45.220
Why are you sighing, Miyuki-chan?

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:47.970
I'm embarrassed to be saying this at this age...

00:10:47.970 --> 00:10:50.430
As embarrassed as I was about the contacts matter...

00:10:50.430 --> 00:10:52.850
...but I've been avoiding the dentist's because it terrifies me...

00:10:52.850 --> 00:10:55.010
...and I got a cavity the other day...

00:10:55.520 --> 00:10:58.730
It even hurts when I drink water.

00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:02.740
Isn't that...

00:11:02.740 --> 00:11:04.100
...normal?

00:11:04.100 --> 00:11:05.660
I'm pretty scared of the dentist's myself.

00:11:05.990 --> 00:11:07.950
But why did you avoid the dentist's...

00:11:07.950 --> 00:11:09.740
...until your teeth started hurting?

00:11:15.290 --> 00:11:16.630
Strangely enough...

00:11:16.630 --> 00:11:19.630
Even when I know that my teeth will end up hurting...

00:11:19.630 --> 00:11:22.760
You still don't want to go to the dentist's, right?

00:11:23.380 --> 00:11:25.010
When the pain first starts...

00:11:25.010 --> 00:11:27.050
...you choose not to go to the dentist's...

00:11:27.050 --> 00:11:29.930
...while you can still live with the pain.

00:11:30.200 --> 00:11:32.220
Is the dentist really that scary?

00:11:32.220 --> 00:11:34.230
I've never needed to go so I don't know.

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:36.020
You've never gone to the dentist's?

00:11:36.020 --> 00:11:37.730
Lucky you...

00:11:37.730 --> 00:11:40.400
There's that hospital smell...

00:11:40.400 --> 00:11:42.670
Or the nerve-wracking wait.

00:11:42.670 --> 00:11:43.610
Ooh! Ooh!

00:11:43.610 --> 00:11:46.110
And the sound of the drill gets me every time!

00:11:46.110 --> 00:11:46.860
Change Getter!

00:11:46.860 --> 00:11:48.580
It's terrifying!

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:51.870
But guys probably like to go to the dentist's, right?

00:11:51.870 --> 00:11:52.410
Why?

00:11:52.410 --> 00:11:54.750
Aren't drills like a man's romance?

00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:56.210
Dinosaur Empire!

00:11:56.400 --> 00:12:00.880
I've heard they love it when robots fight using drills!

00:12:03.300 --> 00:12:06.760
But they probably don't like having their teeth drilled...

00:12:07.000 --> 00:12:08.800
I've been wondering...

00:12:08.800 --> 00:12:11.470
Aren't the receptionists and assistants...

00:12:11.470 --> 00:12:12.770
...usually pretty ladies?

00:12:13.020 --> 00:12:15.020
Now that you mention it, it does seem that way...

00:12:15.430 --> 00:12:16.600
Wonder why...

00:12:16.600 --> 00:12:19.770
Perhaps it's one of their hiring criteria...

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:22.610
Exclusively beautiful assistants and drills, huh?

00:12:29.900 --> 00:12:33.580
That does indeed sound like
something geared towards males.

00:12:33.580 --> 00:12:34.080
Then...

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:36.830
What would a dentist's office for females be like?

00:12:37.180 --> 00:12:40.210
You'd have to get rid of that smell first.

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:45.340
And switch the patient's chair for a soft, auto-massaging recliner.

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:48.260
Then they should also utilize aromatherapy, right?

00:12:48.260 --> 00:12:51.260
And include a foot massage while you're being treated.

00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:54.180
That sounds nice.

00:12:54.180 --> 00:12:58.390
And to numb the pain, they let you play games.

00:12:58.390 --> 00:13:00.480
It might be a little difficult to play games at the same time...

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:03.570
But it's a good way to distract you from the pain.

00:13:03.570 --> 00:13:07.180
They could give you headphones and play your favorite songs.

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:07.990
Sounds good.

00:13:07.990 --> 00:13:09.530
That would also be nice.

00:13:14.080 --> 00:13:17.200
But I still don't like the dentist's.

00:13:17.200 --> 00:13:18.410
That's true.

00:13:18.600 --> 00:13:19.420
What's this?!

00:13:19.740 --> 00:13:20.790
What's wrong?

00:13:20.790 --> 00:13:21.330
Well...

00:13:21.330 --> 00:13:24.040
They're animating another series I like...

00:13:24.040 --> 00:13:27.590
...but they're using a completely
different cast from the drama CD.

00:13:28.420 --> 00:13:29.630
Don't get it.

00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:33.390
Was this the work of a higher power?

00:13:33.390 --> 00:13:34.050
Personal issues?

00:13:34.050 --> 00:13:34.640
Money?

00:13:34.930 --> 00:13:37.770
I never buy drama CDs...

00:13:37.770 --> 00:13:39.390
...so as long as the voices match the original characters...

00:13:39.390 --> 00:13:41.400
...I don't care who they use.

00:13:41.580 --> 00:13:43.860
It doesn't work that way, Kagami.

00:13:43.860 --> 00:13:46.480
People who have gotten used to the drama CD...

00:13:46.480 --> 00:13:49.530
...feel like something's wrong when they start watching the anime.

00:13:49.530 --> 00:13:52.660
It takes a while for the feeling to go away.

00:13:53.990 --> 00:13:54.830
Well...

00:13:54.830 --> 00:13:56.870
...there's one good thing that comes out of this.

00:13:56.870 --> 00:13:57.910
What's that?

00:13:58.100 --> 00:13:59.750
Drama CD and anime.

00:13:59.750 --> 00:14:02.540
You can enjoy two different worlds through them.

00:14:02.540 --> 00:14:03.960
Two for the price of one.

00:14:04.500 --> 00:14:06.500
You're a die-hard fan, huh?

00:14:07.170 --> 00:14:08.510
Thank you very much!

00:14:08.670 --> 00:14:09.170
Well...

00:14:09.170 --> 00:14:14.260
One of us will be taking Miyuki-san's leftover nugget...

00:14:14.570 --> 00:14:17.310
Let's say it goes to whoever wins a staring contest.

00:14:17.310 --> 00:14:17.890
Wha—

00:14:17.890 --> 00:14:19.140
You're like a little kid.

00:14:19.140 --> 00:14:20.390
A staring contest?

00:14:20.390 --> 00:14:21.560
That sounds fun!

00:14:21.560 --> 00:14:23.520
Kagami's probably gonna lose.

00:14:23.520 --> 00:14:24.520
Did you say something?

00:14:24.650 --> 00:14:25.690
Then let's go...

00:14:25.690 --> 00:14:26.980
Stare-down!

00:14:33.740 --> 00:14:34.660
That was...

00:14:34.660 --> 00:14:36.030
...so bad!

00:14:36.030 --> 00:14:37.120
Wow...

00:14:37.740 --> 00:14:38.540
You...

00:14:38.540 --> 00:14:40.040
You didn't
even look human!

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:42.750
Hey, you guys
are overreacting.

00:14:42.790 --> 00:14:44.420
Sorry to have kept you waiting.

00:14:44.420 --> 00:14:45.960
There was a long line for the restroom.

00:14:46.630 --> 00:14:47.960
Did something happen?

00:14:47.960 --> 00:14:48.750
Hey.

00:14:48.750 --> 00:14:51.380
Show that face to Miyuki!

00:14:51.380 --> 00:14:52.470
No way.

00:14:52.470 --> 00:14:54.130
It was incredible, Miyuki!

00:14:54.130 --> 00:14:56.720
I've never seen anything like it!

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:57.880
Fine then.

00:15:02.770 --> 00:15:04.960
It's amazing every time I see it!

00:15:04.960 --> 00:15:09.240
That face may come in handy
during the talent stage of entrance exams.

00:15:09.240 --> 00:15:10.730
That's it, Konata!

00:15:10.730 --> 00:15:12.150
It'll get you into college!

00:15:12.150 --> 00:15:13.570
Guaranteed!

00:15:14.110 --> 00:15:16.160
I'm not exactly thrilled.

00:15:16.440 --> 00:15:20.660
There was this thing on TV about the average
number of books a person in Japan reads annually...

00:15:20.660 --> 00:15:25.040
...and they said to omit manga and limit the count to normal books.

00:15:25.040 --> 00:15:26.170
Well, manga's...

00:15:26.380 --> 00:15:28.500
Do light novels count?

00:15:29.290 --> 00:15:30.500
I'm not sure.

00:15:30.500 --> 00:15:32.670
Light novels should be okay...

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:34.380
What about picture books?

00:15:36.590 --> 00:15:39.050
Since they're called books, they might count...

00:15:39.300 --> 00:15:45.390
Other fantasy stuff like Harry Potter is considered normal...

00:15:45.810 --> 00:15:48.570
So what do you call a normal book?

00:15:50.900 --> 00:15:53.280
And the TV show ended by saying...

00:15:53.280 --> 00:15:57.530
...how young people are becoming increasingly illiterate...

00:15:57.700 --> 00:16:01.160
...but doesn't browsing the Internet and blogging...

00:16:01.160 --> 00:16:05.330
...actually improve your literacy?

00:16:06.670 --> 00:16:09.040
I get it, and then I don't...

00:16:09.300 --> 00:16:09.880
Yo.

00:16:09.880 --> 00:16:11.170
Let's get going.

00:16:11.170 --> 00:16:12.300
Wait one minute.

00:16:12.900 --> 00:16:13.590
Sorry.

00:16:13.590 --> 00:16:15.530
I can't go home with you guys.

00:16:16.050 --> 00:16:17.590
Do you have something to do?

00:16:17.590 --> 00:16:18.300
That's unusual.

00:16:19.200 --> 00:16:21.210
I started working.

00:16:23.950 --> 00:16:24.850
<i>Wait!</i>

00:16:24.850 --> 00:16:26.390
<i>She actually got a job!</i>

00:16:26.390 --> 00:16:28.480
<i>Is Comp Festival really that important?!</i>

00:16:30.500 --> 00:16:31.610
Anyway...

00:16:31.610 --> 00:16:33.610
Konata sure surprised me.

00:16:33.610 --> 00:16:34.900
She sure did.

00:16:34.900 --> 00:16:37.200
She really got a job.

00:16:37.200 --> 00:16:38.860
I thought she was just joking.

00:16:39.660 --> 00:16:41.410
That's also true...

00:16:41.910 --> 00:16:45.020
...but I was talking about how somebody actually hired her.

00:16:45.020 --> 00:16:46.750
Th-That's a little harsh...

00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:47.830
Besides...

00:16:47.830 --> 00:16:51.290
I can't picture her doing manual labor.

00:16:51.290 --> 00:16:52.750
Th-That's true...

00:16:53.050 --> 00:16:55.290
I wonder where she's working.

00:16:55.290 --> 00:16:57.130
Maybe at a bookstore?

00:16:57.130 --> 00:16:58.260
Since she likes manga?

00:16:59.470 --> 00:17:00.220
Excuse me.

00:17:00.220 --> 00:17:00.680
I'd like this.

00:17:00.680 --> 00:17:01.720
Hold on.

00:17:01.720 --> 00:17:03.510
I'm busy right now.

00:17:06.060 --> 00:17:07.180
Ka-ching!

00:17:07.430 --> 00:17:09.270
I hope she doesn't get fired...

00:17:09.770 --> 00:17:11.100
Then how about a convenience store?

00:17:11.980 --> 00:17:12.650
Excuse me.

00:17:12.650 --> 00:17:13.370
I'd like this.

00:17:14.320 --> 00:17:16.420
Fourhundredninetyeightyen.

00:17:17.700 --> 00:17:19.280
Exactchange.

00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:22.120
Thankyoupleasecomeagain.

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:24.370
Doubt it.

00:17:24.370 --> 00:17:25.790
Then what about a fast food place?

00:17:25.990 --> 00:17:27.290
I'm smiling. Gotta problem with it?

00:17:27.290 --> 00:17:28.660
I don't see it happening...

00:17:28.660 --> 00:17:30.790
I guess that also eliminates a family restaurant.

00:17:30.790 --> 00:17:31.790
Welcome.

00:17:32.330 --> 00:17:34.420
I wonder where she's working.

00:17:35.630 --> 00:17:37.170
Traffic survey?

00:17:37.170 --> 00:17:38.090
No way.

00:17:38.090 --> 00:17:39.340
Video rental store?

00:17:39.340 --> 00:17:40.510
Not too sure about that.

00:17:40.510 --> 00:17:41.300
A bar.

00:17:41.300 --> 00:17:42.390
Nah.

00:17:42.390 --> 00:17:43.260
Pizza delivery.

00:17:43.260 --> 00:17:44.300
No driver's license.

00:17:44.300 --> 00:17:45.640
Supermarket cashier.

00:17:45.640 --> 00:17:46.140
Impossible.

00:17:46.140 --> 00:17:47.060
Cram school teacher.

00:17:47.060 --> 00:17:47.890
Unthinkable.

00:17:47.890 --> 00:17:48.930
A bread factory!

00:17:49.350 --> 00:17:50.190
That leaves...

00:17:52.020 --> 00:17:53.520
Let's ask her tomorrow.

00:17:53.940 --> 00:17:54.940
Hey, Konata.

00:17:54.940 --> 00:17:57.120
Where're you working?

00:17:57.120 --> 00:17:58.260
Tell us!

00:18:00.200 --> 00:18:02.340
Just a normal costume café.

00:18:02.910 --> 00:18:04.700
<i>It fits her so perfectly!</i>

00:18:04.700 --> 00:18:05.990
<i>But should she really be working there?</i>

00:18:11.700 --> 00:18:13.000
Good lucky!

00:18:13.580 --> 00:18:14.920
I'm Akira Kogami!

00:18:14.920 --> 00:18:17.340
This is the second episode of Lucky Channel!

00:18:17.340 --> 00:18:19.920
Akira's going all-out!

00:18:20.260 --> 00:18:21.170
O-kay!

00:18:21.170 --> 00:18:22.300
Next to me...

00:18:22.300 --> 00:18:25.050
...we have my wonderful assistant!

00:18:25.050 --> 00:18:26.890
Minoru Shiraishi-san!

00:18:26.890 --> 00:18:28.520
Take it away!

00:18:28.810 --> 00:18:30.140
For-For-For-For—

00:18:30.140 --> 00:18:33.020
I'm Akira-sama's assistant, Minoru Shiraishi.

00:18:33.020 --> 00:18:34.650
I'm just a beginner...

00:18:34.650 --> 00:18:37.020
...so I hope that you'll just remember my name.

00:18:37.020 --> 00:18:37.610
Yes.

00:18:37.610 --> 00:18:39.100
Clap. Clap. Clap.

00:18:39.480 --> 00:18:40.000
Okay!

00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:42.490
This segment's only just begun...

00:18:42.490 --> 00:18:46.660
...but we already have an eruption of messages from everyone!

00:18:46.660 --> 00:18:48.580
Akira's super happy!

00:18:48.580 --> 00:18:49.450
Thanks!

00:18:49.450 --> 00:18:50.000
Man...

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:51.910
This is really something.

00:18:51.910 --> 00:18:52.710
I suppose you could call this...

00:18:52.710 --> 00:18:54.710
...an indication of Akira-sama's popularity.

00:18:55.960 --> 00:18:57.000
Wha—

00:18:57.000 --> 00:18:57.960
What?

00:18:57.960 --> 00:18:59.300
I saw today's episode.

00:18:59.300 --> 00:18:59.920
Yes?

00:18:59.920 --> 00:19:00.760
Didn't you show up?

00:19:01.260 --> 00:19:02.800
In the actual show.

00:19:02.800 --> 00:19:04.090
You were in it, weren't you?

00:19:05.220 --> 00:19:06.600
They were gracious enough to put me in.

00:19:08.340 --> 00:19:10.180
Whatever.

00:19:10.180 --> 00:19:11.560
Oh, yeah...

00:19:11.560 --> 00:19:13.850
What scene were you in again?

00:19:14.100 --> 00:19:15.850
Uh, I believe...

00:19:15.850 --> 00:19:17.520
...scene 45 in part A.

00:19:17.520 --> 00:19:19.150
The classroom scene right after vacation.

00:19:20.900 --> 00:19:22.110
Now I remember.

00:19:22.110 --> 00:19:24.840
You didn't have much of a presence so I forgot.

00:19:25.360 --> 00:19:27.910
Well, I only had one line this time.

00:19:27.910 --> 00:19:29.080
Whazzat?!

00:19:29.080 --> 00:19:29.790
Not good enough for you?!

00:19:30.290 --> 00:19:31.290
No! Absolutely not!

00:19:32.370 --> 00:19:34.890
Not sure a newbie should be actin' that way.

00:19:35.300 --> 00:19:37.790
Y'know, back when I debuted...

00:19:39.340 --> 00:19:40.670
Debuted?

00:19:40.670 --> 00:19:42.120
How old were you then?

00:19:42.630 --> 00:19:43.630
Three.

00:19:43.630 --> 00:19:46.930
I was happy just to get any lines then.

00:19:46.930 --> 00:19:48.890
Quantity isn't the issue.

00:19:48.890 --> 00:19:50.010
You're absolutely right.

00:19:50.010 --> 00:19:53.310
My nerves were a wreck after
being surrounded by so many veterans.

00:19:53.310 --> 00:19:54.730
It was an educational experience!

00:19:54.730 --> 00:19:56.450
You were pretty stiff.

00:19:57.020 --> 00:19:58.270
Stiff as a board.

00:19:58.270 --> 00:19:59.770
Ooh, look! I'm an amateur.

00:20:00.100 --> 00:20:01.230
Y'know.

00:20:01.230 --> 00:20:03.400
That was way too yeah...

00:20:03.400 --> 00:20:05.280
Do it again right now.

00:20:06.300 --> 00:20:07.360
Here?

00:20:07.360 --> 00:20:10.000
There's a chance you'll appear again, right?

00:20:10.620 --> 00:20:11.200
I suppose...

00:20:11.200 --> 00:20:13.500
Then you better practice some.

00:20:13.500 --> 00:20:15.160
I'm offering you help here!

00:20:15.710 --> 00:20:16.540
Yes, ma'am!

00:20:16.540 --> 00:20:18.170
Please help me out!

00:20:18.170 --> 00:20:19.210
Gimme the script.

00:20:20.300 --> 00:20:21.960
Which scene was it again?

00:20:21.960 --> 00:20:23.410
Scene 45.

00:20:24.500 --> 00:20:25.300
This one, huh?

00:20:25.300 --> 00:20:27.680
Then I'll be Ms. Kuroi.

00:20:27.680 --> 00:20:28.640
Please do.

00:20:28.640 --> 00:20:30.180
Ready and...

00:20:30.180 --> 00:20:31.140
Action!

00:20:31.640 --> 00:20:32.470
Howdy.

00:20:32.470 --> 00:20:34.890
Did y'all have a fun vacation?

00:20:34.890 --> 00:20:35.930
Then again...

00:20:35.930 --> 00:20:37.440
You had b-b—

00:20:37.440 --> 00:20:38.400
Bunches.

00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:38.440
You had b-b—

00:20:38.440 --> 00:20:39.560
Bunches of homework...

00:20:39.560 --> 00:20:41.770
...and a test right after vacation...

00:20:41.770 --> 00:20:45.110
...so you couldn't've been having fun the whole time.

00:20:45.110 --> 00:20:47.770
It barely felt like a vacation.

00:20:50.740 --> 00:20:51.490
What was that?

00:20:52.400 --> 00:20:53.450
No good at all.

00:20:53.450 --> 00:20:55.870
That line had no feeling to it.

00:20:55.870 --> 00:20:56.370
Feel—

00:20:56.370 --> 00:20:56.960
Here!

00:20:56.960 --> 00:20:57.410
Right here!

00:20:57.410 --> 00:20:59.290
You gotta make 'em feel it right here!

00:20:59.290 --> 00:21:00.040
I'm sorry.

00:21:00.040 --> 00:21:03.000
If you're just gonna read your lines, a monkey could handle that.

00:21:03.000 --> 00:21:04.670
A monkey can't...

00:21:08.340 --> 00:21:10.430
It's time to say goodbye!

00:21:10.430 --> 00:21:11.890
Time just flies...

00:21:11.890 --> 00:21:14.010
...when you're happy, right?

00:21:14.200 --> 00:21:15.220
And so...

00:21:15.220 --> 00:21:20.440
Send us any questions or comments about the show please!

00:21:20.770 --> 00:21:22.650
We'll see you next time.

00:21:22.650 --> 00:21:24.900
Bye-bye!

00:21:25.600 --> 00:21:26.440
So yeah.

00:21:26.440 --> 00:21:28.030
What were the regulars like?

00:21:28.030 --> 00:21:29.530
What do you mean?

00:21:29.530 --> 00:21:31.030
Y'know...

00:21:31.030 --> 00:21:32.620
Does it look like anyone's going to get knocked off?

00:21:32.620 --> 00:21:34.620
Aren't they all like fighting with each other?

00:21:34.620 --> 00:21:35.410
No...

00:21:35.410 --> 00:21:37.080
It didn't look that way to me...

00:21:37.080 --> 00:21:38.870
Then you're supposed to...

00:21:41.170 --> 00:21:42.960
You're amazing, Kona-chan!

00:21:42.960 --> 00:21:44.420
You were very passionate.

00:21:44.420 --> 00:21:45.500
Hey, Konata!

00:21:45.500 --> 00:21:47.460
Are the other two songs like this?

00:21:48.300 --> 00:21:50.470
There's anime stuff along with the SFX stuff.

00:21:50.470 --> 00:21:52.300
That's not what I meant!

00:21:52.300 --> 00:21:54.550
Sing something the rest of us know!

00:21:55.260 --> 00:21:57.270
I can sing whatever I want.

00:21:57.270 --> 00:21:57.930
Let's see...

00:21:57.930 --> 00:21:59.270
Here's the remote.

00:21:59.270 --> 00:22:00.350
Come on, Tsukasa.

00:22:00.350 --> 00:22:01.310
If you don't order a song...

00:22:01.310 --> 00:22:04.810
...we'll end up listening to her
endless medley of anime songs.

00:22:04.810 --> 00:22:06.780
I'm okay with that.

00:22:06.780 --> 00:22:08.740
This is actually quite fun.

00:22:08.740 --> 00:22:10.490
Even you, Miyuki?!

00:22:10.900 --> 00:22:11.910
Sorry if I block anyone's view.

00:22:11.910 --> 00:22:13.110
I'm gonna stand this time.

00:22:13.110 --> 00:22:14.780
Now what?

00:22:14.780 --> 00:22:15.950
If you don't stand up when you sing...

00:22:15.950 --> 00:22:18.290
...your voice can't truly shine.

00:22:18.290 --> 00:22:20.160
You're gonna sing even louder?!

00:22:22.540 --> 00:22:23.720
Actual footage from the show!

00:22:24.130 --> 00:22:25.340
This is kinda cool!

00:22:25.340 --> 00:22:28.090
Looks like it was made way before we were born.

00:22:47.190 --> 00:22:48.780
Here are your drinks!

00:22:49.900 --> 00:22:51.260
Thanks.

00:22:53.700 --> 00:22:54.920
Who ordered the oolong tea?

00:22:55.320 --> 00:22:56.530
That's me.

00:22:56.530 --> 00:22:58.160
The iced lemon tea?

00:22:58.160 --> 00:22:59.290
That would be mine.

00:22:59.290 --> 00:23:00.620
The orange juice?

00:23:00.950 --> 00:23:01.830
Over here.

00:23:01.830 --> 00:23:03.300
The ginger ale?

00:23:04.330 --> 00:23:05.170
Sorry.

00:23:05.170 --> 00:23:07.170
Could you just set it over there?

00:23:10.920 --> 00:23:14.300
Well, next time on Lucky Star:

00:23:14.300 --> 00:23:15.180
I'm Kagami.

00:23:15.180 --> 00:23:16.850
When you buy juice from a vending machine...

00:23:16.850 --> 00:23:19.760
...and put in a 200 yen coin and get back a
50 yen coin and a 10 yen coin as change...

00:23:19.760 --> 00:23:21.060
...it's like, winner!

00:23:21.060 --> 00:23:22.270
But when you ride the train...

00:23:22.270 --> 00:23:23.890
...and try to buy a 150 yen ticket...

00:23:23.890 --> 00:23:26.690
...and put in a 100 yen coin
thinking that you have five 10 yen coins...

00:23:26.690 --> 00:23:29.360
...but once you put in four, you find out you're short one.

00:23:29.360 --> 00:23:31.360
Since you have no choice, you put in another 100 yen coin...

00:23:31.360 --> 00:23:33.400
...and get back nine 10 yen coins...

